5. gosdt-guesses (BSD-3-Clause) — renamed SPOT
   https://github.com/ubc-systopia/gosdt-guesses

    Vendored into `src/shinrin/_spot/` and renamed **SPOT** (SParse OpTimal;
    formerly exported as `GOSDTClassifier`, now `SPOTClassifier`): the GOSDT
   C++ engine
   ("Fast Sparse Decision Tree Optimization via Reference Ensembles",
   AAAI 2022; "Generalized and Scalable Optimal Sparse Decision Trees",
   ICML 2020) and its Python layer. Upstream's pybind11 module is replaced
   by PyO3 bindings in `src/lib.rs`; oneTBB container types are replaced by
   lock-based shims written for shinrin (`cpp/tbbshim/`, no TBB code) and
   the engine's global `Queue` class is renamed `GosdtQueue` to avoid a
   linker symbol collision with CORELS' `Queue`.

   Copyright (c) 2020-2024, UBC Systopia Lab.
   License: BSD-3-Clause (see src/shinrin/_spot/LICENSE)

6. treeFARMS (BSD-3-Clause) — renamed SPOTSET
   https://github.com/ubc-systopia/treeFarms

   Vendored into `src/shinrin/_spotset/` and renamed **SPOTSET** (Sparse
   Optimal Rashomon Trees): the Rashomon-set enumeration engine
   ("Exploring the Whole Rashomon Set of Sparse Decision Trees", NeurIPS
   2022). treeFARMS is built on the same gosdt-guesses lineage as item 5,
   so its engine is wrapped in `namespace spotset` and co-linked with SPOT
   in one extension. Upstream's pybind11 module is replaced by PyO3
   bindings in `src/lib.rs`; the timbertrek visualization dependency and
   the pure-Python imbalance/OSDT variant are intentionally not ported.

   Copyright (c) 2022, UBC Systopia Lab.
   License: BSD-3-Clause (see src/shinrin/_spotset/LICENSE)

